Aim
To perform data aggregation and apply statistical functions in Tableau for better data analysis.

Description
Data aggregation combines multiple records into summary values. Common statistical measures
include sum, average, minimum and maximum. Tableau can perform these operations directly on
data fields.

Uses
• Finding total sales.
• Calculating average values.
• Finding minimum and maximum values.
• Comparing categories.
• Summarizing large datasets.

Algorithm
1. Open Tableau Public.
2. Connect to the dataset.
3. Drag required fields into rows and columns.
4. Apply aggregation functions.
5. Use statistical measures.
6. Analyze and save the results.

Program
 import pandas as pd
 # Load dataset
 data = pd.read_csv("sales_data.csv")
 # Total Sales
 print("Total Sales:", data["Sales"].sum())
 # Average Sales
 print("Average Sales:", data["Sales"].mean())
 # Minimum Sales
 print("Minimum Sales:", data["Sales"].min())
 # Maximum Sales
 print("Maximum Sales:", data["Sales"].max())
 # Group by Category
 print("\nSales by Category:")
 print(data.groupby("Category")["Sales"].sum())

 Program Explanation
• sum() calculates the total sales.
• mean() calculates the average sales.
• min() finds the minimum sales value.
• max() finds the maximum sales value.
• groupby() groups records according to Category.
• The final sum() calculates sales for each category.

Libraries / Functions Used
Pandas: Used for aggregation, statistical calculations and grouping data.

Sample Output
The output displays total sales, average sales, minimum sales, maximum sales and sales grouped

